Item 02 is done. Six items remain unchecked, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE` line.

**What was built.** `learning/fingerprint.py` classifies the sub-collection from structure-only features under three splits, tests the same thing at equal size, predicts Chu & Stuckey's density class with a seed-index control, and draws the UMAP map at `reports/figures/instance_space.png`. Section 2 of `reports/ml_nature.md` records the results, with the raw tables in `reports/fingerprint_tables.md`. Seven new tests pass and the full suite is green (710 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed, 72 s). Nothing was written to `solutions/`, no solver default changed, nothing committed.

**The finding.** The benchmark families are fingerprintable and the fingerprint is not size.

- Structure alone assigns 94.4% of instances to their collection with the file held out, 93.3% with isomorphic copies held out too, and 98.8% at equal size against a 61.6% baseline.
- Size alone scores below the majority class under a grouped split, and size-free features match the full set.
- The rule is readable. Every Harvey instance has constant column sums, constant row sums, or both, and no other generator has either. Faggioli–Bentivoglio caps its largest product at half the customers. Simonis is dense with large products. Chu & Stuckey is sparse where nothing else is, and its density class is recovered from mean customers per product alone at 98% while the seed index sits at chance.
- Shaw, Miller, Wilson and the Challenge copies cannot be fingerprinted because each is one file or one size. Their byte-copies set a ceiling of 0.993 that the model hits exactly.
- The map is a lattice of 74 size cells, not a continuum. The 24 industrial SCOOP instances have almost no SCOOP neighbours and fall in the sparse region shared with all 200 Chu & Stuckey instances.

**Two method traps caught and documented in the module.** Gradient boosting scored 0.81 on a random split where a random forest scores 0.98, thrown by the one- and twenty-instance classes. Unshuffled GroupKFold on the sorted Chu & Stuckey filenames held out one seed index per fold and made the control score exactly zero. Both were replaced.

**Next.** Item 03, node counts into the ledger. PROGRESS.md notes that later grouped studies should use the file-plus-graph-class grouping now in `learning.fingerprint.union_groups`, and that SCOOP is the natural held-out test for transfer to real instances.

